# Source stays diffable (anton-flih).
#
# `diff` forces git to render a patch for these globs instead of falling back to
# `Binary files differ` when it finds a stray control byte. Every reviewer here — human, Codex,
# Claude, anton's own pre-PR review — reads diffs, so a file git calls binary is a file nobody
# reviews; that is how a bug reached main in epic-graph.ts (anton-74f8).
#
# `text` is deliberately NOT set. It would also switch on end-of-line normalisation: a no-op today
# and a surprise for a Windows checkout later. Diffability is what this buys; nothing else.
#
# The `Binary files differ` alarm this retires is replaced, not deleted, by the `control-bytes` CI
# gate — `bun run check:control-bytes` (src/lib/control-bytes.ts). Keep the globs below in step with
# SOURCE_EXTENSIONS there; control-bytes.test.ts fails when they drift.
#
# See .product/decisions/2026-09-05-source-diffability.md.

*.cjs   diff
*.css   diff
*.html  diff
*.js    diff
*.json  diff
*.md    diff
*.mjs   diff
*.sh    diff
*.sql   diff
*.svg   diff
*.toml  diff
*.ts    diff
*.tsx   diff
*.yaml  diff
*.yml   diff
